# Witness: private hides each declaration given to it as an argument: a callable does not find a or b among the names of
# its caller, so its input a is unknown (3), and seen is not written. The same without private: marks_code_dynamic_public.
# Norm: the book #private-binding, #qualification; the author 2026-11-18 #marking-receivers-execute.
# Slice M1 (plan #one-graph-plan): the declarations of a field under its modifiers.
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: peek () int
    return: a * 10 + b
sub: main () (
    int: k 0
)
    private: int: a 1; int: b 2
    shared\Observed\seen := peek()
main()
